course: dictionary
lesson: 5318
title: Ken: a Scots word for know
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: In Scotland and Northern England, people say «I dinnae ken» instead of «I don't know». Dinnae is Scots for don't, so ken must mean know. The words around ken give you the clue.
explain: Ken can also be a verb with changing forms: ken, kens, kent or kenned. You will meet it often in Scottish stories and poems, so it helps to recognise it.
explain: Ken has a second, more formal meaning. «Rocket science is beyond my ken» means it is outside what I know or understand. You will mostly see this phrase in books.
explain: At the end of a sentence, «It was brilliant, ken» means you know. Ken is also a boy's name, short for Kenneth. Check the sentence each time to see which meaning fits.
fact: Ken means know in Scotland and Northern England: «I dinnae ken» means I don't know.
fact: Ken is a verb that changes: ken, kens, kent or kenned, kenning.
fact: «Beyond my ken» means outside what I know or understand.
fact: At the end of a sentence, «ken» means you know, as in «It was brilliant, ken.»
fact: Ken is also a boy's name, short for Kenneth.
exercise: «I dinnae ken where my bag is.» What does ken mean here? | *Know | Hide | Sing | Forget
exercise: Ella reads «Rocket science is beyond my ken.» What does beyond my ken mean? | Very high up in the sky | Far away from my house | Something I love very much | *Outside what I know or understand
exercise: «It was brilliant, ken.» What does ken mean at the end of this sentence? | *You know | Hidden | Kenneth, a boy's name | A kind of small boat
test: In «She kent the answer all along», which word is a form of ken? | *kent | along | she | answer
test: Which sentence uses ken to mean you know? | «Rocket science is beyond my ken.» | «I dinnae ken where he went.» | *«It was brilliant, ken.» | «Ken is a boy's name.»
exam: What does «I dinnae ken» mean? | I am called Kenneth | Yes, I know it well | *I don't know, since dinnae is Scots for don't | I can see the sea
